A||||13||Standard||Dead battery?||||11
Z||000000||Standard||11-07-1999||07:01 PM||||Alright guys, I need some help...<P>I drove my car to Winona, 2.5 hour drive, 135 miles, and it ran fine... started it up about 5 hours later to go to mcdeath, ran fine.  Went out to start it today, after it had been sitting for about a day and a half, and the battery was dead.   took the battery out to get it tested, at Tire's Plus they said the voltage was around 8 volts, and that 1 or 2 of the cells were probably shorted.  Took it to Fleet Farm, where I bought it, and they said said they would have to charge it to test it.  They charged it, and it put out 681 cranking amps (it's rated at 650).  Put it back in my car and it started up right away... to say the least, I'm confused...  anybody have any ideas?<P>Thanks..||||reg||11
Z||000001||fierospeeder||11-07-1999||07:54 PM||||What was your voltage reading?  while the car is runing.  It should be 14.  If it is that means the car is charging the battery.  Otherwise it will show a 12.  If its 12, you can have a loose belt, only on the non serpentine belt setup, i got a 2.5L which does get lose.  Or your alternator is bad.  You can take those in to a parts shop and they can run to see if its making 14volts. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||11-08-1999||03:15 AM||||I just got home and the car ran fine the whole way...  The voltmeter on the dash reads 15, the voltage at the battery is around 14 volts...  I'm just totally confused...||||reg||8
Z||000003||fierospeeder||11-08-1999||03:20 AM||||you might have left something on, unless someone else knows what can be draining it.  See what happens today if its the same.||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||11-08-1999||03:28 AM||||Yeah,8 volts is pretty low,I'd keep a set of jumper cables around for a few days until you figure it out.Make sure it's full of water,even if you have to peel the sticker away from the removable portion/lid.<BR>Actually sounds like it might be a bad connection.<p>[This message has been edited by lowCG (edited 11-08-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||88 Fiero||11-08-1999||10:23 AM||||Also after checking everything that you could possibly think that can cause this problem and it's still exist...just change the batteries co'z the cells might be bad... It happened on my car...I keep bringing it back and forth to the auto parts and keep showing okay..ti'll I decided to replace it with a new one...no more problems of battery being dead...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Rodrv6||11-08-1999||03:51 PM||||Hi, I'm new to this forum, but I had the same problem last year with my 84 SE.  The battery kept going dead overnight, but tested O.K.  The alternator was putting out 14.5 volts.  I discovered one of the alternator diodes had shorted internally and was draining the battery.  A rebuilt alternator solved the problem!||||reg||1
Z||000007||sinoloa||11-08-1999||11:38 PM||||once the cell is dead in the battery, it won't hold a charge.  ||||reg||7
Z||000008||sinoloa||11-08-1999||11:47 PM||||Here's a way to check if a wire is shorted or dragging the battery down.  Connect and disconnect the positive battery terminal several times and check to see if you have any sparks coming from the disconnecting and reconnecting process.  Make sure all your switches and ignition is off, all your doors closed, etc.  There shouldn't be any sparks. If there's a spark, you have something that is on, and that could be what's draining the battery.  I think you'll have to pull the ECM fuse out, too, but I'm not sure.||||reg||3
Z||000009||Standard||11-09-1999||01:04 AM||||I'm gonna replace my alternator soon,  I just need the money... My car started up fine today, when I put the key in w/o cranking the engine the voltmeter on the dash went to 13, as usual.  I did have the cigarette lighter adapter for my discman plugged in, but that's been in since I bought the car over a year ago.  The battery is barely 6 months old.  I'm just gonna leave it alone for now.. it seems that as soon as I try to fix one thing my car throws another problem at me..  Thanks for all the help, though!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Mike||||reg||1
