Z||000011||kornholio||11-09-1999||06:52 PM||||hey Formula,<BR>what's starting fluid?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Carrolles||11-09-1999||09:59 PM||||Occasionally a battery plate will become slightly loose inside the battery and touch the adjacent plate temporarily shorting out the cell.  This will give a low voltage reading.  The plate will often move back in place and test fine until the plate moves again, usually due to temperature or shock.<P>Through the years I've had this happen many times as batteries approach the end of their useful life.<P>I learned many years ago that it didn't matter how expensive a battery I bought I always seemed to get about three years life out of them.  I finally quit buying 60 and 72 month batteries only to have to get it replaced on a pro-rated basis after about 36 months.<P>I've been buying Walmart batteries for the last to years or so and have had no trouble with any of them.  After three years when they are about shot I go to Walmart and get another.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Carrolles||11-09-1999||10:00 PM||||My last paragraph should havee said for the last ten years, not the last to years.<BR>Sorry||||reg||1
